untime activation is needed for those proofs.\n\nCANDIDATE SET:\nExamined 16 of 16 changed paths at inventory/search level; this is **not** 16 whole-file reviews:\n\n- `mercury.config.json` — configuration excerpt and identity verification.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/adversarial-review.js` — complete diff and selected caller/receipt ranges.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/ask.js` — selected dispatch, metadata and CLI ranges; supplied diff excerpts.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/codex-challenger.js` — complete source.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/config.js` — complete diff and configuration excerpts.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/consensus.js` — complete diff.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/doctrine-review.js` — complete diff.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/llm-client.js` — complete diff and selected legacy/new-client ranges.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/provider-preflight.js` — complete source.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/reviewer-panel.js` — complete source and diff.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/run-ledger.js` — complete diff and selected consumers.\n- `test/mercury-astra-challenger.test.js` — complete selected-tree blob.\n- `test/mercury-consensus.test.js` — partial diff and lexical scan.\n- `test/mercury-llm-config-contract.test.js` — lexical scan; diff delivery incomplete.\n- `test/mercury-provider-preflight.test.js` — partial diff and lexical scan.\n- `test/mercury-reviewer-panel.test.js` — delivered diff and lexical scan.\n\nAdditional candidates: historical Fable compatibility, Mercury/Kimi routing, raw-tape preservation, tool telemetry, model identity, executable trust, transport/readiness reporting, relevant `CHANGELOG.md` matches and older history. Historical replay and exhaustive history remain unresolved. The host’s 11-path inventory omitted five changed test paths.\n\nAST EVIDENCE:\nNo AST tool was used, and no actual AST scan result was supplied. Mercury mislabeled textual diff/search evidence as AST evidence. My inspection used Git object reads, blob hashes, ripgrep and numbered source excerpts. All 11 materialized changed production/configuration files matched the selected tree’s blob identities. Host delivery accounting does not establish my whole-file coverage or Mercury’s reasoning coverage.\n\nINHERITED:\nThe following records distinguish lexical presence from proven violations; unexamined semantics remain unresolved:\n\n- `mercury.config.json`: no literal `|| 0`, catch or bypass-env matches; silent-default behavior requires consumer analysis.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/adversarial-review.js`: no literal `|| 0`; catches, defaults and environment reads present. Examined stage catches preserve failure receipts; remaining catch/default semantics unresolved.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/ask.js`: `|| 0` at 1484, 1566, 1704; catches, defaults and environment reads present. Full swallowed-catch/bypass/default audit incomplete.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/codex-challenger.js`: newly added, not inherited; no `|| 0`; parse catches record errors at 36 and 43; fallbacks and environment handling present. Trust defect described above.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/config.js`: no `|| 0`; catches, optional defaults and environment controls present; full semantic classification incomplete.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/consensus.js`: no lexical matches for the four requested categories.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/doctrine-review.js`: executable `|| 0` at 133 and 194; line 16 mentions the pattern in doctrine text. Defaults present; no environment match; semantic audit incomplete.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/llm-client.js`: no `|| 0`; parsing/error catches, defaults and environment reads present. Legacy alias restrictions are not an Astra defect.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/provider-preflight.js`: no `|| 0` or environment match; catch at 204 records failures; defaults present. Inherited unconditional success becomes incorrect with the new returned-error contract.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/reviewer-panel.js`: no `|| 0` or environment match; catch at 245 records failed seats; defaults present.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/run-ledger.js`: `|| 0` at 342 and 479–481; catches, defaults and environment reads present; full semantic audit incomplete.\n- `test/mercury-astra-challenger.test.js`: no lexical matches; newly added.\n- `test/mercury-consensus.test.js`: catches and environment references present; no literal `|| 0`; semantics incompletely examined.\n- `test/mercury-llm-config-contract.test.js`: catches and environment references present; no literal `|| 0`; semantics incompletely examined.\n- `test/mercury-provider-preflight.test.js`: no lexical matches.\n- `test/mercury-reviewer-panel.test.js`: no lexical matches.\n\nFOURTH SHAPE CLASSIFIER:\nClassified 8 of 8 **host-listed throw candidates**; this is not a complete census of every added conditional/fallback:\n\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/adversarial-review.js:805`: inherited missing-review-object guard with renamed message; caller supplies the review object through `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/ask.js:1409`.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/adversarial-review.js:1237`: retained hard-boundary rethrow after fallback removal; producer is the stage error at `:1174`, classifier at `:30`.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/config.js:473`: provider configuration boundary; producer `:456`.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/config.js:476`: endpoint configuration boundary; producer `:457`.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/config.js:479`: credential-routing boundary; producer `:460`.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/config.js:482`: configurable-command restriction; producer is the configuration property inspected at `:481`.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/config.js:485`: requested-model restriction; producer `:458`.\n- `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/config.js:488`: removes emergency-model routing; producer `:459`.\n\nThese concern review infrastructure, not bot-runtime authority. The six configuration throws replace existing restrictions. Mercury’s “missing alias guard” classification does not identify an added guard.\n\nALLEGATIONS:\n- Alias-matcher break: SUBSTANTIVE; TESTIMONY; contradicted by inspected caller evidence.\n- Executable-trust regression: MECHANICAL; RECEIPT; selected-source control flow.\n- False provider readiness after transport failure: MECHANICAL; RECEIPT; selected-source producer/consumer chain.\n- Exhaustive-coverage and AST claims: MECHANICAL; TESTIMONY checked against delivered tool receipts; unsupported.\n\nSUBSTANTIVE RESOLUTION:\nUNRESOLVED-FOR-TREY. Mercury asserts an alias-matcher break; this reviewer rejects that allegation and identifies two distinct defects. No Kimi adjudication or Mercury response to this challenge was supplied.\n\nWHAT I EXAMINED:\nSelected-tree changed-path inventory, production-file blob identities, source/diff ranges listed above, new Astra test source, reference searches, changelog matches, Mercury’s complete supplied answer, tool failures and host coverage diagnostics.\n\nDID NOT EXAMINE:\nEvery whole file, every historical era, complete historical Fable receipts, actual installed executable provenance, live provider tapes, or complete test execution. Four test diffs were delivered with truncation. Five tests are absent from the materialized snapshot; immutable Git objects supplied their inspected content. No host-attested test/build result was supplied.\n\nASSUMED:\nNo assumption that the executable is actually compromised, that a timeout occurred in production, or that a model-sandbox check establishes test authority.\n\nWHAT I DID:\nPerformed read-only source inspection and traced concrete producer-to-consumer consequences. Verified the 11 materialized changed source/configuration blobs against the requested tree.\n\nWHAT I DID NOT DO:\nEdit files, invoke another reviewer/provider, execute tests, change runtime state, or complete an exhaustive historical audit.\n\nWHAT I ASSUMED:\nThe reported failure scenarios are reachable inputs to the inspected code, not observed production incidents.\n\nWHY THIS VERDICT:\nTwo concrete replacement defects are supported independently of Mercury’s refuted allegation. Missing coverage does not establish those defects or erase their source evidence.\n\nIF INCOMPLETE, WHY:\nWhole-file/history coverage and trusted execution proofs remain incomplete. Supplied HTTP 503/504 failures, malformed/unaccepted ingestion units, truncated deliveries and the unwritten Mercury ledger remain diagnostics—not code verdicts or test results."},"sequence_number":2826}
